Proposal only (not applied, not built). Scope: scaled (draw_resolution_scale > 1)
readback-resolve path. The downscale reads from the start of the *current scaled
range* (copy_dest_base * scale_area) but writes guest memory at written_address
(= copy_dest_extent_start). When the two differ (resolve to a sub-rectangle /
offset destination), the CPU-visible copy is shifted. The unscaled branch already
copies from written_address. This does NOT by itself prove a KI-038/KI-032 fix;
it removes one scale-only CPU-visible corruption source and should be tested
with the A/B in ki-038-032-analysis.md.

